WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.928
Connection strings need lifecycle management.

2
00:00:02.928 --> 00:00:13.340
Every sensitive connection string should have an owner, purpose, environment, system, data classification, privilege level, storage location, and rotation path.

3
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:17.895
Without inventory, teams cannot rotate confidently or respond quickly.

4
00:00:17.895 --> 00:00:27.721
Rotation should be planned so applications, connection pools, background jobs, migrations, and dependent services continue operating during transition.

5
00:00:27.721 --> 00:00:30.909
Some systems may support overlapping credentials.

6
00:00:30.909 --> 00:00:36.506
Others may require coordinated deployment, pool clearing, restarts, or phased cutover.

7
00:00:36.506 --> 00:00:39.499
The plan should be tested before it is urgent.

8
00:00:39.499 --> 00:00:45.746
Revocation should be fast enough for the risk of the system and should be tested where possible.

9
00:00:45.746 --> 00:00:56.353
A high-privilege credential, a customer-data system, or an internet-facing application may need a faster response path than a low-sensitivity development database.

10
00:00:56.353 --> 00:00:58.891
Risk should drive timing and ownership.

11
00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:07.350
Stale credentials, unused database users, old app settings, abandoned service principals, and copied secrets should be cleaned up.

12
00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:15.029
Old access paths create confusion during audits and can remain active long after the application no longer needs them.

13
00:01:15.029 --> 00:01:27.913
Suspected exposure response should include containment, disabling or rotating credentials, reviewing logs, identifying affected data and systems, notifying owners, and documenting follow-up actions.

14
00:01:27.913 --> 00:01:35.201
The response should preserve useful evidence while keeping the secret value out of broad communication channels.

15
00:01:35.201 --> 00:01:42.750
Backup, restore, rollback, and disaster recovery plans should account for connection string and secret availability.

16
00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:47.240
A restore plan that cannot access the required secrets is incomplete.

17
00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:55.309
A rollback plan that restores old app configuration may accidentally restore old credentials unless the process is reviewed.
